digicarlo (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The window is now a cartoon car. The shots sit in a landscape seen
    through the windshield, and the controls live on the dashboard of a
    Nash Metropolitan, the way Putt-Putt's did: the cameras and cards in
    the glove box, a horn that honks and looks for cameras again, a radio
    whose preset keys date the selected shots, a fuel gauge for free space,
    a clock, and a big red START button.
  * The paint is the Metropolitan's actual Caribbean Blue (PPG P-905,
    Ditzler 41161), paired with Snowberry White, instead of a generic
    powder blue.
  * Text is anti-aliased and strokes are at least two pixels wide. The
    unsmoothed 8-point font of 1.0 came out thin and broken on Wayland at
    fractional scales such as 150%.
  * The UI font is Nunito; fonts-nunito is now recommended.
  * Sounds: the horn honks, and a finished job beeps twice. View > Sounds,
    or 'digicarlo config set sounds no', turns them off.

 -- antair <antairdo@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0000

digicarlo (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * First release.
  * Pulls from memory cards (mounted read-only through udisks when the
    desktop has not mounted them), PTP cameras through gphoto2, the SiPix
    Blink II through Blinky 1.6.1's driver, and any folder.
  * Every file is archived byte for byte and read back before it counts;
    a file a failing card will not give up is reported and the rest carry on.
  * Dates come from when the pictures came off the camera. Sessions are
    found where the camera's clock was reset, the gaps within each are kept,
    and any run of shots can be given its own start or keep the camera's
    date.
  * MOV, AVI and MTS clips are remuxed to MP4 with the video stream copied
    bit for bit, checked by hashing it in both files; 8-bit PCM and other
    audio MP4 cannot hold becomes AAC.
  * digicarlo-gui: Windows 95 dressed as a Nash Metropolitan.

 -- antair <antairdo@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
